I got the same problem.  NH308PC1.UU produces a self extracting Zip file called
"NH308PC1.EXE".  I ran it after I got the warning from UUdecode, and I got a
"Error in ZIP - Use PKZipFix."  So, I used PKZipFix on it, and it made a file
called PKFIXED.ZIP.  I unzipped that, and got NETHACK.000 with _no_ errors.
Unzipped the other half (NH308PC2.EXE) and it made NETHACK.001.  Then I ran the
SPLITF.EXE program that came with it as, "SPLITF nethack /r" and it put the two
files into one, and made a (big) NETHACK.EXE.
After all that (took 10 minutes to figure it all out).  I ran Nethack and (to
my surprise), it worked!  I'm happily playing 3.0pl8 now.
